camchrome: canvas and WebGL noise is idempotent, stays in the clip, and toBlob carries it.

A seed sweep of the Clearcote audit found three readback contradictions, seed-dependent:

- "readPixels writes only the pixels it was asked to read": the noise loop clipped rows but not
  columns, so a readPixels region larger than the framebuffer got noise outside it (reproduced on
  every seed tried). Columns, and the uniformity check's rows, now stay in the clip.
- "a canvas reads back the same through toDataURL and getImageData" and the WebGL readPixels vs
  toDataURL row: the audit decodes the PNG by drawing it into a second canvas and reading it with
  getImageData, which applies the noise again. The noise flipped a bit keyed on the full value,
  so the second pass re-keyed every pixel the first one changed and moved a few again. It now keys
  on each channel without its low bit and SETS that bit, so noise over noised pixels is a no-op
  and every exit agrees exactly, however often pixels go round.
- toBlob/convertToBlob: ImageDataBuffer::EncodeImage noised with seed 0 (not the per-site seed),
  and the progressive encoder did not noise at all, so blobs disagreed with toDataURL. The blob
  source is now noised once, per site, when the blob creator is made; EncodeImage adds nothing.

